{
  "phase": "ERROR-CONTRACT-V1",
  "purpose": "Expected Torneos domain errors must answer as 4xx with their functional code, never as an outage. Single source of truth for migration 00000000000006_domain_error_contract.sql (built by build-migration.mjs), its rollback, the gateway's legacy-SQLSTATE defense (torneos-gateway/competition.ts DOMAIN_ERROR_STATUS) and the lab certification (integration/torneos-core-contracts/error-contract.test.mjs); guard tests keep them equal.",
  "root_cause": [
    "PostgREST v14.15 answers SQLSTATE 55000 / 55P03 / 54000 / P0002 (and INTO STRICT) with HTTP 500.",
    "PostgREST retries SQLSTATE 40001 (serialization_failure) inside the same request: a deterministic domain 40001 is re-raised thousands of times until the gateway gives up at 5 s and answers 503.",
    "torneosTransport.js treated any status >= 500 as an outage: it dropped the bridge bearer, threw TORNEOS_UNAVAILABLE and lost rpcError, so the UI showed 'Torneos no disponible' for ordinary conflicts."
  ],
  "postgrest": {
    "version": "v14.15",
    "custom_status": "RAISE ... USING errcode = 'PTxyz' answers HTTP xyz with the unchanged { code, message, details, hint } body (code = 'PTxyz'); measured in the lab before writing the migration.",
    "legacy_5xx_sqlstates": [
      "55000",
      "54000"
    ],
    "retried_sqlstates": [
      "40001"
    ]
  },
  "semantics": {
    "400": "invalid domain input (P0001 / 22023 / 23514, unchanged)",
    "403": "permission / domain authorization (42501, unchanged)",
    "404": "only when no existence leak (none introduced)",
    "409": "stale state, conflict, already exists, read-only lifecycle",
    "422": "valid request refused by a domain limit",
    "429": "rate limit"
  },
